**Instructor**  
**Professor:** Mary Anne Smart  
**E-Mail:** [masmart@purdue.edu](mailto:masmart@purdue.edu)  
**Office Hours:** Tuesday, 2:30pm – 3:30pm in DSAI 1119D or by appointment  

**Graduate Teaching Assistants (GTAs)**  
- **Sai Coumar**  
  **E-Mail:** [scoumar@purdue.edu](mailto:scoumar@purdue.edu)  
- **Shrutheesh Iyer**  
  **E-Mail:** [iyer270@purdue.edu](mailto:iyer270@purdue.edu)  
- **Pinaki Mohanty**  
  **E-Mail:** [pmohanty@purdue.edu](mailto:pmohanty@purdue.edu)  

### Contact Information for Resources

For additional resources and support, please contact the Office of the Dean of Students:
- Phone: [765-494-1747](tel:7654941747)
- Hours of Operation: Monday to Friday, 8 AM – 5 PM

### Mental Health Services

Purdue University is dedicated to the mental health and well-being of its students. If you or someone you know is struggling with feelings of being overwhelmed, depressed, or in need of mental health support, please reach out to Counseling and Psychological Services (CAPS):
- Phone: [765-494-6995](tel:7654946995) (available during and after hours, including weekends and holidays)
- Location: Second floor of the Student Health Center (PUSH) during business hours.

### Basic Needs Security

Any student facing challenges with securing food or housing is encouraged to contact:
- Office of the Dean of Students: [odos@purdue.edu](mailto:odos@purdue.edu)
- Basic Needs Program: [basic-needs@purdue.edu](mailto:basic-needs@purdue.edu)

Student Support Services are available Monday to Friday, 8 AM – 5 PM.

### Emergency Preparation

In the event of a major campus emergency, course requirements, deadlines, and grading percentages may be subject to change due to a revised semester calendar or other uncontrollable circumstances. Relevant changes will be communicated through the course website or can be obtained by reaching out to instructors or TAs via email. It is essential to frequently check your Purdue email for updates.

### Tentative Course Schedule for CS 44100 - Data Science Capstone

**Introduction (2 weeks)**:  
- Discuss CRISP-DM and its phases while selecting and settling on projects.

**Business and Data Understanding (4 weeks)**:  
- Explore projects and identify necessary information to address arising questions. Teams will plan their time schedule for the upcoming weeks. Reports and presentations will be required.

**Data Preparation (3 weeks)**:  
- Format data for analysis purposes. Reports and presentations will be required.

**Modeling (4 weeks)**:  
- Experiment with different modeling techniques using the team's data. Reports and presentations will be required.

**Evaluation (Remainder of Semester)**:  
- Assess the effectiveness of the model, possible success, and learning outcomes. Reports and presentations will be required.

### Disclaimer

This syllabus is subject to change. Any changes will be announced on Brightspace.
