Tutor List Overview
The Department of Mathematics at Purdue University does not employ tutors directly but maintains a list of qualified individuals interested in tutoring. This list is available for students seeking assistance in various math courses. International students should note that federal law prohibits them from outside employment, which includes being on the tutor list. Those interested in being added to the list can complete a survey provided by the department.
__________________________________________________
Reporting Concerns
Students are encouraged to report any significant issues or concerns regarding the tutors listed. Concerns can be directed to Tim Delworth, who will consider them for future tutor list publications.
__________________________________________________
Tutor Information
The following is a list of available tutors, including their contact information, hourly rates, and the specific Purdue math courses they are qualified to tutor. Some tutors also offer services to high school students.

