### Textbook
- **Recommended:** Database System Concepts, 7th Edition by Avi Silberschatz, Henry F. Korth, and S. Sudarshan.
  - ISBN (Paperback): 978-1260084504
    - [Amazon Link](https://www.amazon.com/dp/126008450X)
  - ISBN (eTextbook, hardcover, or loose-leaf): 978-0078022159
    - [Amazon Link](https://www.amazon.com/dp/0078022158)

The textbook webpage provides additional resources such as slides, answers for practice questions, and an SQL interpreter at [db-book.com](http://www.db-book.com).

### Lectures
- **Meeting Times:** 
  - Indianapolis: **MW 5:30 PM to 6:45 PM**, ET 202.
  - West Lafayette: **TuTh 10:30 AM to 11:45 AM**, BHEE 129.

Lecture slides will be available at least one hour before the lecture. Recordings will be posted on Brightspace unless technical issues occur. They may be available as one or multiple videos. A subset of slides will be posted a few days after lectures. Note that solutions to in-class quizzes are not included in the posted materials. All class content is copyrighted.

### Course Schedule with Activity Due Dates
- **Schedule Information:** The schedule is tentative and subject to change. Due date changes will be highlighted in red.
  - View the schedule here: [Course Schedule](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1mov5_UbuG9F6wt_QZWm8yGn4kfpkYqokqkzzgk0kwOU/edit?usp=sharing)

### Course Content and Links
- **Brightspace:** Content such as the syllabus, course schedule, lecture slides, and lecture videos will be uploaded to Brightspace. Quizzes and submission for some homework assignments will also be conducted via Brightspace.
- **Ed:** Class announcements and student questions will be posted on Ed. Students can use Ed to ask questions.
- **Gradescope:** Some homework assignments will require submissions via Gradescope. Notifications for submissions will be provided on Ed and during lectures.

### PSO Schedule
- PSOs will begin in the second week of the semester. Attendance is optional.
- **Locations:** 
  - Indianapolis: SL 247
  - West Lafayette: HAAS G050
- PSO schedule will be posted at the end of week 1.

### Communication Protocol
- **Course Ed Group Registration:** Sign up using this link: [Ed Signup](https://edstem.org/us/join/Ym5mMG) 

Communication from the Instructor and TAs:
- Class announcements will predominantly be made via Ed.

Communication from You to the Instructor and TAs:
1. Discuss questions with classmates.
2. Use the search feature on Ed before posting questions to find similar inquiries.
3. Post a public question on Ed. Anonymity is an option for asking and answering.
4. Attend office hours for direct interaction with the instructor or TAs.
5. Use private questions on Ed for sensitive issues, but note responses may be less immediate. 

### Important Notes
- Public questions will be prioritized. For personal queries, consider rephrasing them for public discussion.
- This structure is designed to encourage peer engagement and maximize the learning environment.
