 Information Technology Services Overview
Purdue University offers a range of IT services to support students, faculty, and staff. Key areas include learning spaces, software access, and remote instructions for software usage. The services are primarily designed for instructional purposes and are restricted to West Lafayette campus students.


__________________________________________________
 Software Remote Instructions
To access software remotely, users must connect through the Purdue VPN if not on the PAL 3.0 Wi-Fi. The steps to connect are as follows:
1. Open the Citrix Workspace application (available for download if not pre-installed).
2. Enter the Store URL: goremote.itap.purdue.edu.
3. Log in using your career account credentials (no Duo authentication required).
4. Select the desired software from the Apps menu once the application loads.

If issues arise, users are advised to try the web-based light version of the software. The home directory for Purdue Career Accounts will be accessible as drive W: on the Software Remote server.


__________________________________________________
 Troubleshooting for Software Remote
For any difficulties encountered while using the Software Remote system, users are encouraged to submit a request via the Purdue IT Service Portal for assistance.


