### CS 24000 - Programming In C  **Instructor:** Christopher K. May  **Course Description:** CS
24000 focuses on the C programming language, emphasizing programming techniques, software
development, and problem-solving strategies. The course is designed to help students become
proficient in writing and debugging C programs.  ### Key Topics May Include: - Basics of C
programming - Control structures (if statements, loops) - Functions and modular programming - Arrays
and strings - Pointers and dynamic memory management - Structures and file operations  ###
